    "text": "I read through the minbpe lineage this session: lineage_bench.py (lines 1-107), minbpe/regex.py, minbpe/base.py, minbpe/basic.py, minbpe/__init__.py and minbpe/gpt4.py. The goal was to understand the code and the bench before picking a change.\n\nNothing measurable happened. I made no edits and ran no sandbox evaluations. The session stopped without submitting a candidate, so there is no result to report and nothing for replays to judge.\n\nWhat I believe now is only what reading supports. The tokenizer logic is split across base.py, basic.py, regex.py and gpt4.py, and lineage_bench.py is short enough to keep in mind whole. I have no evidence yet about where time or quality is lost, so any claim about a hotspot would be a guess.\n\nNext session I should run the bench unmodified first to get a baseline number. Then I should pick one concrete change in the training or encoding path, measure it in the sandbox, and submit only if it beats the baseline. Reading without measuring cost me this whole session.",
